# OSM Leech Lattice Tiles - Status Report

## Date: 2026-02-20

## Objective
Create OSM planet tiles with 24D Leech lattice encoding, Monster Group symmetry, and rich attributes (wikidata, highway, amenity). Output as compressed Parquet files.

## Problem
- JSONL writer works but produces 527 GB uncompressed (57 GB compressed)
- Parquet writer OOMs because it buffers all nodes in memory before writing
- Parquet format doesn't support append - must write complete files

## Solution: Write Parquet in Chunks

### Approach
1. Buffer nodes per tile up to 10K chunk size
2. Write chunk to temporary Parquet file
3. At end, merge all chunks per tile into final Parquet

### Memory Constraints
- Available: 17 GB
- Threads: 8 parsers + 8 writers = 16 threads
- Buffer: 10K nodes per tile × 4,189 tiles = max 41M nodes
- Each LeechNode: ~500 bytes
- Max memory: 41M × 500 = 20 GB (TOO MUCH)

### Better Approach: Write Chunks Immediately
- Buffer only 1K nodes per tile
- Write chunk when tile reaches 1K nodes
- Merge chunks at end per tile
- Max memory: 4,189 tiles × 1K nodes × 500 bytes = 2 GB ✓

